  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Bart and two of his friends pooled money together to buy a bottle of blueberry juice whose unit price is $$12.50$ per gallon. How much juice should Bart get if he only puts in $1$ dollar?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$12.50$ per gallon (dollars per gallon). To find the amount of blueberry juice that Bart could get for $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in gallon per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n12.50\\,\\text{dollars per gallon}\\,\\to \\,1÷12.5=0.08\\,\\text{gallons per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.08$ gallons per dollar. Therefore, Bart should get only $0.08$ gallons of the blueberry juice.",
